{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>If I have sharpened the lightning of My sword.</b> If I make the blade of My sword shine so that it has lightning; שפלנ״דור בְּלַעַ״ז." "<b>And My hand holds fast the measure of justice.</b> To set aside the attribute of mercy from My enemies who did harm to you — ״for I was wroth a little, and they helped for evil״ (Zechariah 1:15) — and My hand holds the attribute of justice, to grasp it and take vengeance." "<b>I will render vengeance.</b> Our Sages learned in the aggadah from the language of Scripture, which says <b>and My hand holds fast the measure of justice</b> — unlike the attribute of flesh and blood is the attribute of the Holy One, blessed be He: flesh and blood shoots an arrow and cannot bring it back, but the Holy One, blessed be He, shoots His arrows and it is in His power to bring them back, as though He holds them in His hand — for His arrow is the lightning, as it says here <b>the lightning of My sword, and My hand holds fast the measure of justice</b>. And this 'measure' is a term for punishment; יושטיצ״א בְּלַעַ״ז."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French esplendeor, 'brilliance/shine'", 2 "the la'az is Old French justice, 'justice/judgment'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:32.257973218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}